  "details": "I previously modified the Grabbing by Side switch of the VIVE Controller to function in \"Toggle\" mode using the Steam Controller Configuration, instead of the default \"Button\" or \"Trigger\" modes.\n\nIn the current build, when I configure the side switch to \"Toggle\" mode as before, the gesture can be toggled, but the Udon system fails to recognize Grab input from the Side Switch.\n\nNOTE: VRC Pickup works well now as like before.\n\nHowever, when set back to the default \"Button\" mode, the udon system can recognize the Side Switch Input.\n\nWhat I want to do is to keep Grabbing only once trigger the Side Switch in Game worlds to reduce my burden on hands, and it was possible in previous build.\n\nThus, I believe this is a bug of the kind of Udon input related to the Side Switch Input in current build.\n\nThank you.",
